menu "csi-hello"

config CSIHELLO_WIFI_SSID
    string "AP SSID to join"
    default "myssid"
    help
      Any 2.4 GHz AP will do for a first smoke test - it does not have to be
      the dedicated sensing AP yet. The point of this app is only to prove
      that this board produces CSI at all.

config CSIHELLO_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "AP password (empty for an open network)"
    default ""

config CSIHELLO_CHANNEL_HINT
    int "Channel hint (0 = let the driver scan)"
    range 0 14
    default 0

config CSIHELLO_PRINT_EVERY_N
    int "Print one line per N CSI callbacks"
    range 1 1000
    default 1
    help
      At close range a busy channel can produce hundreds of callbacks per
      second, which floods the UART and makes the output unreadable. Raise
      this to thin the printout. The counters printed on each line are of
      ALL callbacks, not just printed ones.

config CSIHELLO_AMPLITUDES
    int "How many subcarrier amplitudes to print per line"
    range 0 32
    default 6

endmenu
